Instruction on how you created the tools isolation for this product.
Please include platform you installed on, where you installed it, what
you copied where, etc.:

The Pltform Integration Toolkit provides some services that TDI can make use
of as well as beans for ISMP and IA that make things like adding Linux shortcuts
better supported.  To get the code, the steps involved are:

1.  Download the latest version/fixpack from https://cs.opensource.ibm.com/forum/forum.php?forum_id=10145
    Currently v2.2 fixpack 3: PlatformIntegrationToolkit2.2fp3.zip from

2.  Unzip PlatformIntegrationToolkit2.2fp3.zip into a temporary directory

3.  Check the following files into CMVC:

    All files under GenericWindowsService into adks/ibm/pit/2.2/GenericWindowsService
    All files under InstallShieldCustomBeans/SystemUtilities into adks/ibm/pit/2.2/InstallShieldCustomBeans/SystemUtilities
    InstallShieldCustomBeans/InstallShieldCustomBeans.jar adks/ibm/pit/2.2/InstallShieldCustomBeans

4. If anything in the ISMP project needs to change, like adding an action, append the following 
   to the ismp.registry file found in the installation location of InstallShield.  See the
   readme downloaded with PIT to see if other actions have been added.
   (This is not needed for the installer to build)
      com.ibm.eec.pit.ismp.product.actions.AddSystemGroupWithDeletionOptionAction
      com.ibm.eec.pit.ismp.product.actions.AddSystemUserAccountWithDeletionOptionAction
      com.ibm.eec.pit.ismp.product.actions.CreateLinuxDaemonAction
      com.ibm.eec.pit.ismp.product.actions.CreateLinuxShortcutAction
      com.ibm.eec.pit.ismp.wizard.actions.JVMDump
      com.ibm.eec.pit.ismp.wizard.conditions.CredentialCheckCondition
      com.ibm.eec.pit.ismp.wizard.conditions.SystemGroupExistsCondition
      com.ibm.eec.pit.ismp.wizard.conditions.SystemUserAccountExistsCondition
      com.ibm.eec.pit.ismp.wizard.conditions.WindowsAccountHasPrivilegesCondition

   Also note...DO NOT put spaces on the end of theese action names in the registry file as ISMP
   will not recognize them.
 
